    echr:hasCourt doc:conseilDetat ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelCassation ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "54"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Under section 39/67 of the Aliens Act, an appeal on points of law against the decisions of the Aliens Appeals Board lies to the Conseil d’État ."@en .

doc:conseil_detat_17may2018 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Conseil d’État judgment of 17 May 2018 dismissing the administrative appeal on points of law"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_appeals_board_24mar2017 ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2018-05-17"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelCassation ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "23"^^xsd:string,
        "27"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "An administrative appeal on points of law lodged by the applicants against that judgment was dismissed by the Conseil d’État on 17 May 2018."@en,
        "An appeal on points of law against this judgment was dismissed by the Conseil d’État in a judgment of 17 May 2018, on the same grounds as those set out in the above-cited judgment of the same date (see paragraph 23 above)."@en .

doc:proceedingAdministrativeCourtsChallengeAliensOffice a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "proceedings before the administrative courts to challenge the refusal by the Aliens Office to issue them with visas"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceedingAliensOfficeRefusal ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:authorityAdministrativeCourts ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "8"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "For its part, the Belgian State opposed, before the same courts, the granting of visas."@en,
        "they brought proceedings before the administrative courts to challenge the refusal by the Aliens Office to issue them with visas."@en .

doc:proceeding_brussels_court_of_appeal_2016_12_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "the Brussels Court of Appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_aliens_appeals_board_2016_10_20 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:authorityBrusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-12-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeClaimGranted ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionFavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "75"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the Brussels Court of Appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016 ordering the Belgian State to execute the Aliens Appeals Board’s judgment of 20 October 2016"@en .

doc:proceeding_conseil_detat_applicants_2018_02_08 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Conseil d’État dismissal of applicants' appeal on points of law (8 February 2018)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_aliens_appeals_board_lift_stay_2017_03_06 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:conseilDetat ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2018-02-08"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelCassation ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "17"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 8 February 2018 the Conseil d’État dismissed an appeal on points of law by the applicants against the judgment of 6 March 2017. It held that no departure from the case-law had been made out and dismissed the arguments in which the applicants alleged a breach of the principle of legal certainty and a violation of Articles 3 and 13 of the Convention."@en .

doc:proceeding_conseil_detat_state_2018_02_08 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Conseil d’État dismissal of Belgian State's appeal on points of law (8 February 2018)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_aliens_appeals_board_stay_2016_10_07 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:conseilDetat ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2018-02-08"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelCassation ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "18"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On the same date the Conseil d’État dismissed an appeal on points of law brought by the Belgian State against the judgment of 7 October 2016 on the grounds that, following the lifting of the stay of execution on 6 March 2017, the contested judgment no longer adversely affected the Belgian State."@en .

doc:proceeding_long_stay_application_rejected_2016_12 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Application for a visa to stay for more than 90 days rejected (December 2016)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_aliens_office_refusal_2016_09_13 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensOffice ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-12"^^xsd:gYearMonth ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "13"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "The applicants subsequently submitted such an application, which was rejected by the Belgian authorities in December 2016 (see paragraph 34 below)."@en .

doc:urgentApplicationCourtOfFirstInstance a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Article 584 of the Judicial Code provides for the possibility of applying to the president of the court of first instance by means of an urgent application or by an ex parte application:"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliensOfficeRefusal ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:courtOfFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeUnknown ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "56"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote """Article 584 of the Judicial Code provides for the possibility of applying to the president of the court of first instance by means of an urgent application or by an ex parte application:
“The President of the Court of First Instance shall, in respect of all matters except those which the law excludes from the jurisdiction of the courts of justice, give a provisional ruling in cases which he recognises as being urgent.
...
The matter shall be brought before the President by means of an urgent application or, in cases of absolute necessity, an ex parte application.
....”"""@en .

doc:aliensAppealsBoardProceeding a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "apply to the Aliens Appeals Board to have the Aliens Office’s decision set aside."@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliensOfficeRefusal ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensAppealsBoard ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "52"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "If the Aliens Office refuses to issue a visa, the requesting party may apply to the Aliens Appeals Board to have the Aliens Office’s decision set aside."@en .

doc:aliens_appeals_board_20oct2016 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "By a judgment of 20 October 2016 the Aliens Appeals Board ordered a stay of execution of the refusal decisions of 17 October 2016"@en ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelAppeal ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "25"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By a judgment of 20 October 2016 the Aliens Appeals Board, essentially reiterating the substance of its previous judgments, ordered a stay of execution of the refusal decisions of 17 October 2016. In addition, in view of the imminent danger faced by the applicants, the Belgian State’s persistent refusal to comply with res judicata authority and the importance of ensuring that the remedy was effective, it considered that it was justified to direct the State to issue the applicants, within 48 hours, with laissez-passers or visas, valid for three months."@en .

doc:aliens_appeals_board_24mar2017 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "On 24 March 2017 the Aliens Appeals Board dismissed the application to have those decisions set aside"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_appeals_board_20oct2016 ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2017-03-24"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelAppeal ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "22"^^xsd:string,
        "26"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By a judgment of 24 March 2017 the Aliens Appeals Board dismissed the application to have the decisions set aside and ordered that the stay of execution in respect of the visa refusal decisions be lifted, together with the interim measures, based on the same reasoning as that set out in its first judgment of the same date (see paragraph 22 above)."@en,
        "On 24 March 2017 the Aliens Appeals Board dismissed the application to have those decisions set aside, finding that the Aliens Office’s decisions of 13 September 2016 (see paragraph 11 above) had become final and that, in consequence, the applicants no longer had standing to challenge the subsequent decisions."@en .

